            {
                "entry_id": "3a348ca0-f537-3a42-85ee-4d24fc0aea82",
                "word": "Moloch",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5c791f30-bdc2-48d1-b0a3-fa3e5febf58b",
                        "entry_id": "3a348ca0-f537-3a42-85ee-4d24fc0aea82",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Molochs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "65722e51-e5fc-3c1d-857b-0c18642c1263",
                        "entry_id": "3a348ca0-f537-3a42-85ee-4d24fc0aea82",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dieu auquel les Ammonites, une ethnie cananéenne, sacrifiaient leurs premier-nés en les jetant dans un brasier."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0b450f14-b581-4ecc-9bbe-e3139c2e193c",
                                "sense_id": "65722e51-e5fc-3c1d-857b-0c18642c1263",
                                "text": "Les vrais dieux antiques sont certainement Baal et l’affreux Moloch, voilà des dieux naturels ! … Baal dieu des jouissances, Moloch dieu des tortures."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5d60201-09a9-4c6c-89f1-b72a44ce182a",
                                "sense_id": "65722e51-e5fc-3c1d-857b-0c18642c1263",
                                "text": "– Toutes ces fourmis noires, gargouillantes de café-crème, qui s’engloutissent chaque matin dans les bouches du métro comme les Carthaginois dans la gueule du Moloch, vous ont donné mauvaise conscience…"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cc237e7e-2f1c-3c07-beed-130d468d9291",
                        "entry_id": "3a348ca0-f537-3a42-85ee-4d24fc0aea82",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Genre qui comprend une espèce, le moloch (Moloch horridus), une espèce de lézard."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bd73fb0c-9b31-4baf-bbc3-bcd99a161a50",
                        "source_entry_id": "3a348ca0-f537-3a42-85ee-4d24fc0aea82",
                        "target_lang_word": "Moloch",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Moloch",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3fa9ad3c-5499-3cb8-8b80-ef7ccb30489f",
                                        "entry_id": "6113520f-60f9-3bf7-b4ae-0b3249db2aee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ancient Ammonite deity worshiped by the Canaanites, Phoenician and related cultures in North Africa and the Levant, often depicted with the head of a bull."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "70eef460-c8a6-3cda-b8e2-fc5b4a455455",
                                        "entry_id": "6113520f-60f9-3bf7-b4ae-0b3249db2aee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person or thing demanding or requiring a very costly sacrifice."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a04ad9bd-bb3c-4149-93e8-674857d21148",
                                                "sense_id": "70eef460-c8a6-3cda-b8e2-fc5b4a455455",
                                                "text": "[W]e can't without wonder remember that horrid Invention projected in this place, but thanks be to God diſappointed, wherein there was not Reverence to the ſacred Bones of Princes, but all were at one blaſt to be offer'd up to Moloch."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d9b3438-b48b-4866-9c22-708c593fa882",
                                                "sense_id": "70eef460-c8a6-3cda-b8e2-fc5b4a455455",
                                                "text": "They [bankers] would do what has been done by the Bank of France—buy bullion at a premium, on the approach of danger, and keep peril at a safe and respectable distance. Any expenditure that might be incurred for that purpose would be small indeed when contrasted with the immense loss and suffering caused by the present system, and the continual fear in which the public now live of some new crisis—because it has been out of one and into another for a long period now; and that will be the case hereafter, until we have no interval to gather strength, and recruit for the next struggle with Mammon, or Moloch, or whatever other name of evil import belongs to the \"Tutelarity\" of Lombard-street and its precincts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d154b681-43f4-42a1-8910-b629eac466e0",
                                                "sense_id": "70eef460-c8a6-3cda-b8e2-fc5b4a455455",
                                                "text": "[…] poor Johnny Tetterby staggering under his Moloch of an infant, the Juggernaut that crushes all his enjoyments."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8f676ffa-da37-416e-961a-aece990e5963",
                        "source_entry_id": "3a348ca0-f537-3a42-85ee-4d24fc0aea82",
